        "On customs, since 28 March 2025 the AES has applied a 0.5% confederal levy on imports from third countries, exempting AES products, humanitarian aid and goods in transit. Sources differ on whether it applies to goods from ECOWAS countries outside WAEMU, and no collected amounts have been published. Mali, Burkina Faso and Niger also remain members of WAEMU and the BCEAO zone, together with Senegal, Côte d'Ivoire, Togo, Benin and Guinea-Bissau. For these five countries, the customs and monetary union absorbs most of the institutional shock. The net gain from a framework agreement is therefore concentrated in relations with Nigeria, Ghana and Guinea."
